t(23, 1590, """O Muslim men and Muslim women: Our Prophet ﷺ told us about the power of Surat al-Baqarah, but when he spoke he was not addressing the bewitched or those afflicted by touch.

He ﷺ was addressing the healthy who have neither sorcery nor touch, so that the surah would be a protection for them.

There are many cases of the bewitched with strong and severe sorcery relapsing when Surat al-Baqarah is recited, because for them it is no longer a shield and protection, but has become a treatment. The difference between understanding the hadith as protection, which is correct, and understanding it as treatment, which is wrong, is enormous, great and huge. Most of our brothers and sisters did not distinguish between protection and treatment and thought the hadith speaks about treatment.

The hadith speaks about protection.

There are many cases of the strong afflicting entity in the touched person taking revenge because of the recitation of Surat al-Baqarah. Sorcery itself is of many types, forms and colours: there is weak sorcery in which the afflicting entity is weak, there is medium, and there is strong. All of that is by Allah's will and under His decree, for a profound divine wisdom. Therefore no touched or bewitched person knows by himself the strength of the afflicting entity that has settled in him. Cases of great exhaustion after reciting Surat al-Baqarah have been observed in no small number of the bewitched, and cases of the afflicting entity's effect increasing after the patient recites Surat al-Baqarah by himself have also been clearly observed.

Finally, take from al-Baqarah its closing verses as treatment, and focus on the word treatment, because I never understood the noble hadith as treatment; I understood it only as protection for the healthy.

Al-Fatihah, Qul huwa Allahu ahad, the closing verses of Surat al-Baqarah, al-Mu'awwidhatayn, and Ayat al-Kursi.

Whoever among the patients finds strain, fatigue and weariness, let him go to the raqi known for his religion, piety, strength and experience,""")

