t(33, 645, """Take heed, O people of sight and understanding. Each one of these, and I saw them all over the length of my long life, had been exhausted and wearied by the world, then when the lowly world in which we are all tested was opened to them, they forgot the effort and fatigue that had befallen them, and the result of their test pleased them, as they turned into a state in which rejoicing in the blessing came to them. So beware of much joy and delight in the results of the lowly, perishing world, for by Allah it is like one who waits every day and every hour for the command of its Lord: it raises and lowers people, then lowers and raises people, then raises and lowers people. When Allah wills a lowering, He commands it: Lower so-and-so, or lower a whole people. By Allah, there are among people some who were lowered with such a lowering that they wished for a crumb of dry bread, green and full of bacteria, and did not find it, and there are some who were so lowered in it that their health melted away and their wellbeing went, and they wished in it for the body of a weak, feeble old man. So do not glorify it, do not glorify it, and do not glorify your effort in it, and do not glorify what your effort has come to, lest it be a gradual ruin. Whoever's soul glorifies the result of his effort has been led into gradual ruin, and has entered through one of the severest gates of destruction, facing his destruction in it, and his smallness among people after his soul swelled and grew haughty and people glorified him before the blessing was taken from him!""")

